rians were not the first to find  nor keep dragons they utilize them in  ways that no others had before  turning them into weapons of mass  destruction dragons are inherently  magical beings it is said that they are  fire made flesh their lives are many  times that of a man as they age their  scales grow thicker and their dragon  flame grows hotter balerion the black  dread could melt stone and steel with  this black fire dragons are near  invulnerable to fire but not completely  there are cases of dragons being hurt  and even blinded by the flame of other  dragons there is no doubt then there is  some a special connection between the  Valyrian nobility and their dragons this  connection however doesn't seem to be as  solid as the connection between a warg  and a wolf the implications are that the  taming of dragons must in some way  relate to a magical bonding a bond that  is able to be passed down genetically  the phrase blood of the dragon seems to  add weight to this all Valyrian magic  was said to be rooted in fire and blood  so we can only assume that it was some  sort of blood ritual that created the  bond that linked the dragons and the  Valyrians initially knowledge of how to  perform such a thing would obviously  have had to come from the people of the  shadow who for whatever reason must have  taught the Valyrians how to bond  themselves with dragons as well as  various other arts including their  technique of fusing stone and even  possibly the production of Valyrian  steel it seems evident that dragons have  some sort of effect on the potency of  magic in the a Song of Ice and Fire  world there is evidence that the  proximity effects the potency it is easy  to assume that the number of dragons  would also have some effect this all  being said magic performed within the  Valyrian Empire must have been quite  powerful due to the amount of dragons  this would explain better why the  Valerians were able to conquer the East  so quick  they not only had dragon fire but  powerful sorcery as well not much is  known about life within Valyria but we  do know that only noble houses at  dragons it would likely then follow then  magical learning was confined amongst  the highborn the Targaryen however  seemed to not have kept any of the  magical teachings of the lost Empire  strange considering the fact that dragon  stone was built using the Valyrian Way  of fusing stone now lost the Targaryen  s' obviously knew at least some methods  they hatched dragon eggs on dragon stone  as well but why did they not maintain  the knowledge why has knowledge that  kept an empire for millennia faded from  memory after only a few hundred years  perhaps the spells no longer worked  perhaps much of the ancient Valyrian  magic only worked while the Empire stood  the castle dragon stone was built while  the Valyrian Empire still stood it was a  hundred years after Dainius Targaryen  Sproul see that the doom of Valyria came  down there is no evidence of any  Valyrian few stone structures being  built after this point it makes more  sense that the knowledge could have been  lost if the techniques no longer worked  if dragons are the sources of magic in A  Song of Ice and Fire then much of that  power must have been lost when the vast  majority of dragons died in the doom but  still the Targaryen at least had some  dragons but perhaps this was not enough  and also blood was required it is known  that the Valyrians would sacrifice  slaves to work their sorcery slaves were  treated horribly in the Valyrian Empire  it is mentioned that the Targaryen  brought slaves when they initially came  to Westeros but obviously the practice  stopped slavery at the time had been  forbidden in Westeros for thousands of  years since the rise of the faith of the  seven mullerian the dread though adult  at this time wouldn't have been the  legend that he would be a hundred years  later  so perhaps Targaryen less temperamental  than Aegon decided to conform rather  tha